# CNOT-dihedral circuits: the presentation

Amy, Chen and Ross, *A finite presentation of CNOT-dihedral operators*:
the relations `R₁`–`R₁₃` of Figure 1, with the laws of the symmetry (§2)
and the structural rules, present the group of `n`-qubit CNOT-dihedral
operators, the subgroup of `U(2ⁿ)` generated by `ω`, `X`, `T`, `CNOT` (and
`SWAP`), for every `n` (Propositions 3.6, 5.5 and 6.4).
-/
import QCert.CNOTDihedral.Complete

namespace QCert.CNOTDihedral

open Circuit

/-- **The presentation** (Propositions 3.6, 5.5 and 6.4): on every number
of wires, the relations of Figure 1 with the laws of the symmetry present
the group generated by the CNOT-dihedral gates. -/
theorem presentation (n : ℕ) : IsSubPresentationOf (Theory n) (S.gen (n := n)) where
  grouplike := grouplike n
  sound := fun w v h => theory_sound n w v h
  complete := fun _ _ h => complete_pa n (pa_eq_of_sem h)

end QCert.CNOTDihedral
